WEBVTT

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:04.000
The terrorists who targeted the train for Garm

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.290
merged to create an automa through
the power of the primary red gem.

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:06.580
<b><i>Activate</i></b>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:06.580
<b><i>[Primary Red,</i></b>

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.130
<b><i>Armored Knight]</i></b>

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:11.710
Consequently, the train went out of control.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:19.710
I connected myself to the massive amount of ether
in Akari to conjure a major spell and avert disaster,

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:17.290
<b><i>Medium, Menou</i></b>

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:17.290
<b><i>-Etheric Boost-</i></b>

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:17.290
<b><i>Maintain Invoke</i></b>

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:17.290
<b><i>[Kneel before the front gate,</i></b>

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:17.290
<b><i>for its path leads to the Lord.]</i></b>

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:24.790
but my heart is still anxious over a
bizarre sensation I felt during the trip.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:38.670
I see. So you felt it too, Momo? That bizarre sensation?

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:43.130
Yes, I did. I see what you're thinking.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:48.380
You think that was the moment when Boobalicious
used her Pure Concept to turn back time.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:52.710
Akari has the Pure Concept of Time. It makes sense.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:57.380
We were about to crash into the train up ahead,
which would have been a huge disaster.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:02.040
And I have a hunch... that it actually happened once.

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:05.080
And Boobalicious turned back time?

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:09.830
Then you mean she can turn back
time for the entire world as well?

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.250
It seems that way.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
She can turn back just her own time,
or for the entire world at will.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.210
This time for some reason,
she chose to turn the whole world back.

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.710
But why?

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:27.920
Maybe she unconsciously wanted to
save the other passengers as well?

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.960
Her? You really think so?

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.710
That's how ordinary girls think.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:33.670
By the way...

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:36.000
What about the non-ordinary girl
you got tangled up with?

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.250
You mean that crappy little princess?

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:42.040
Honestly, I actually thought about squishing her dead,

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.830
but I did the civil thing and shook her off my tail instead.

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:46.210
You should be proud of me!

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.580
What a good girl. You did a great job.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:46.960
<b>Second Class Carriage</b>

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:50.080
Well then, Momo. I'll see you in Garm.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.420
Hey, Menou?

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.080
What?

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.920
I've said this before,
but please do be careful of Miss Boobalicious there.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.210
<b>Second Class Carriage</b>

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.630
Yes, I know.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.000
There are two days until the ritual for elimination.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.170
I have to make sure she doesn't use her
Pure Concept any more than she already has.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:04.920
Later, then.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.830
Like I said, that's not what I'm worried about...

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:15.290
A Pure Concept that is improperly
attached is perpetually unstable.

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:19.420
It grows the more it's used,
making it even more dangerous.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:21.040
I have to be careful...

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:24.920
To make sure a tragic Human Error never happens again.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:26.250
And...

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.460
To never let there be...

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:34.380
Another one like me from that incident.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:08.790
<b>Episode 4: The Ancient Capital Garm</b>

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:08.330
I don't know what happened to me.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:12.790
All I remembered was my name, "Menou."

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:15.380
I felt no sorrow, no fear.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:17.920
I was simply there.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:25.290
You've always had a flair for flashy maneuvers...

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.000
Orwell you old hag.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:31.000
You haven't changed a bit yourself, Flare.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.290
You do love acting in secrecy.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.960
My role is different from yours.

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:39.880
Leave it. I'm going to look around for survivors.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.250
I'll leave that girl in your hands.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:44.670
Isn't this kind of thing your job?

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:46.630
You recently became a Master, didn't you?

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:49.080
You should take on an unfamiliar task once in a while.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:55.000
Who are you?

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.250
Who am I?

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:07.630
I'm a priestess: pure, just, and strong.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:16.500
Oh?

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.710
So the etheric connect doesn't bother you.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.290
As magecraft material, you're top quality.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.500
So? What do you want to do?

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:29.000
If you have a request I'll at least hear you out.

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.670
I don't have any.

00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:34.920
Of course.

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:38.040
You've been blanched
both physically and mentally, after all.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:56.130
As long as I'm going back that way,
I'll take care of you until the Sanctuary.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.960
If you don't die before then,
you can do what you want after that.

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:05.040
Thus, I ended up traveling for a while with that woman.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:07.540
And at some point,

00:06:07.540 --> 00:06:10.630
I learned that the woman was
what was called an Executioner.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:29.710
I didn't feel anything about that in particular.

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:33.670
Eventually, we arrived at a great continent of salt.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.750
Can you believe it?

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:40.710
They say this used to be one big continent
that was home to multitudes of people.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:46.210
But now everything has turned to salt,
and it's gradually dissolving into the sea.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:50.380
I'm sure it won't be too far off
when it dissolves completely.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:51.960
Look.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:54.080
That's the Sword of Salt.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:58.420
Purification embodied that turns all it pierces to salt.

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:00.330
A sword that can destroy the world.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:04.250
The whole world could have
met the fate of this continent.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:08.710
This is what a Pure Concept can do,
and the Human Error it can bring about.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:11.380
This is the kind of calamity otherworlders can cause.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:12.170
That's why...

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:16.920
The fact that your town was
wiped out is relatively benign.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:26.540
I sensed in that moment that this person had made
the long journey to bring me here just to tell me that.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:31.830
Just so she could give those words to a
girl who had lost all sense of emotion.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.170
This person...

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:41.420
Who had looked blackish red and frightening at first...

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.630
I've decided what I want to do.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:45.580
Oh?

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.080
Let's hear it.

00:07:47.250 --> 00:07:49.540
I want to be you.

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:51.750
I don't understand.

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:54.500
You want to end up like me?

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:57.580
I'm an Executioner. A villain.

00:07:57.670 --> 00:08:01.830
I thought you said you were a priestess
who is pure, just, and strong.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:05.630
Are you so stupid that you don't know what sarcasm is?

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:10.080
You stand up to the kind of thing
that happened to my hometown.

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:12.830
I hate what it became, as well.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:16.750
That's why I want to be like you.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:20.420
If you say you're a villain, then I'll be one, too.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:22.580
Why not become an ordinary priestess?

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:26.250
You might very well become one
that's pure, just, and strong.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:27.630
Right.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:30.790
You're choosing the wrong path.

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:32.540
You can still change your mind.

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:33.920
Right.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:37.830
Idiot.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:46.000
Can I ask what your name is?

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.210
Flare.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:48.210
Actually, no.

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:50.080
You can call me "Master."

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:51.750
Yes, Master.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:57.580
She took me to a convent in the depths of the Sanctuary.

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:02.920
There, I learned many things:

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:06.670
About magecraft, about the nation called Japan,

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:06.670
<b>Japan</b>

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:09.330
and the taboo entities that came from it.

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:12.080
They say our ancient civilization
once dominated the continents,

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:17.460
conquered the seas,
and even went beyond the skies to visit the stars.

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:23.420
That prosperity was made possible by making
rampant use of the otherworlders' Pure Concepts.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:29.330
You can see the extent of our dependency by how their
language became the universal language of our world.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.330
<b>Four Major Human Errors</b>

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:30.750
However...

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:34.830
That civilization perished due to four Human Errors.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.250
<b>Dragon</b>

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.250
<b>The Sword of Salt</b>

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:33.170
<b>Evil</b>

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:33.170
<b>The Pandemonium</b>

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:34.080
<b>Vessel</b>

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:34.080
<b>The Material Room</b>

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.040
<b>Star</b>

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.040
<b>The Starhusk</b>

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.420
It was the result of Pure Concepts evolving out of control.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:41.460
Otherworlders have no means of returning to their world.

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:44.750
And so, the only way to deal with
otherworlders who come to this world...

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:46.880
Is to kill them.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:49.630
We also learned how to kill the taboo entities.

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:54.880
Why do we kill?

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:57.540
Because we are the villains, that's why!

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.630
You think it's for justice? For our faith? For the Lord?

00:09:58.630 --> 00:09:59.210
Next!
You think it's for justice? For our faith? For the Lord?<b></b>

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:00.920
You think it's for justice? For our faith? For the Lord?

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:05.500
No! There is no such vindication!
We don't get to be righteous!

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:09.880
We are resented, hated, and will
eventually get tossed aside.

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:10.960
That's the kind of villains we are!

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.710
So kill them!

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:16.670
Kill any and all otherworlders,
regardless of whether they are good or bad!

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:21.920
Speak of friendship. Whisper words of love.
Be dirty and underhanded to kill them!

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:24.170
Until the day comes when you die...

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:25.080
Kill...

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:26.080
Kill...

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:27.960
And keep on killing!

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:38.790
Stab them? Kill them? What's wrong with everyone?!

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.210
Don't touch me!

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:44.960
I hate people who would tolerate the idea of murder!

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:50.580
There's a new girl who's two years younger
than me who I see crying a lot.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:52.960
So?

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:56.000
I don't think she wants to kill anyone.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:57.880
It's not just her.

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.630
None of the girls here want to do that.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:02.830
Maybe so.

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:04.750
And?

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:09.380
So Master, make me the only bad person.

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:16.540
I'll kill more otherworlders than anyone else,
to make up for that girl and all the others.

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:17.330
So...

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:24.250
Make up for the others? You? Kill?

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:32.670
Menou, you may have value as magecraft material,
but your etheric capacity is below average.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:33.500
Right.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.960
Your physical capabilities are even lower,
although better than the worst.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:37.500
Right.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:41.830
Your mental abilities like memory, mental acuity,
and resourcefulness are so-so.

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:42.920
Just around average.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:43.460
Right.

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:45.880
Your face isn't half bad.

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:49.210
You have the potential to deceive with your charms,
be it man or woman.

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:50.670
A step up from average.

00:11:50.670 --> 00:11:51.420
Right.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.380
Overall, a tad below average.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:58.170
Are you really determined to be
like me with that kind of talent?

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:02.580
Yes, Master.

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:06.250
Don't make me like you. I want to be you.

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:11.580
A villain who has culled the most taboos
in history and is pure, just, and strong.

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.130
I see.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:29.170
An awfully twisted personality has
emerged from your blanched out soul.

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:33.630
Then I will beat everything I know into you.

00:12:33.630 --> 00:12:35.750
And I mean everything.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:37.170
Do you understand?

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:38.540
Yes.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:44.580
Assimilate everything I am into the blank soul of yours,

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:50.630
and when one day all of it is destroyed by
happiness and you still manage to survive...

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:54.170
That's when you'll surpass me.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.080
Yes, Master.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.580
Good answer.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:01.040
To begin, let's do something about
your wretched etheric control

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:04.080
by teaching you how to use etheric camouflage.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:08.170
But before that, you should do something with your hair.

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:11.130
There are plenty of cases where you
can manipulate people with your looks.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:12.920
It's called having a sense of style.

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:15.040
I see. "Style," got it.

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:17.500
Menou, you'd better keep up.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:22.330
From that day forth,
I went through a long, long period of training

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:24.920
to become Master Flare's successor:

00:13:24.920 --> 00:13:26.420
Flarette.

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.000
That's right.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.040
That's the promise I made with Master Flare.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:39.710
I have to kill more otherworlders than anyone,
as many as I possibly can.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:41.710
That's my job.

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:45.920
That was a nice nap!

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:48.130
It's afternoon already, sleepyhead.

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:50.080
What? Really?

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:52.330
Look! We can see it already.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:55.670
Is that Garm?

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.040
Wow!

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:01.920
Yes, that's where the ceremonial hall is
where we can send you back home.

00:14:02.830 --> 00:14:05.000
That's our destination.

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:19.290
What a pretty city!

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:23.130
Isn't it? Garm is famous for its scenic beauty.

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:26.960
Menou, Menou! I want to go see the sights here!

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.080
Oh, together with you, of course!

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:32.080
I think fun things are even better with two people!

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:35.250
Sure. But first, there's a place I need to visit.

00:14:35.420 --> 00:14:38.920
It's a date, okay? You'd better keep your promise!

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:40.210
Fine, fine.

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:44.960
There?! Is that castle where we're going?!

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:46.830
Sorry, but no.

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:48.500
That's the former royal palace.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:52.080
It's Noblesse territory where the royalty,
nobility and knights are.

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:53.630
I have business over that way.

00:14:54.130 --> 00:14:57.880
That's the cathedral, a sacred place for us Faust.

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:02.290
Didn't you say the Faust and
the Noblesse don't get along?

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.130
But they're next to each other?

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:07.580
It's a historic city, so I'm sure there are reasons for that.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:11.040
Anyway, that's where we'll find the
hall we're looking for, apparently.

00:15:11.710 --> 00:15:14.420
Oooh. Woow!

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:15.790
Sooo pretty...

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:18.750
Stop talking. You sound like an idiot, Akari.

00:15:19.330 --> 00:15:21.750
You make some pretty biting
comments sometimes, Menou.

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:24.670
Only because you keep acting like a dummy.

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:28.380
Menou, you're so cold! I'm going home soon, you know?!

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.790
But it really is something, isn't it?

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:34.960
I've never actually been in this cathedral before,
but it's breathtaking.

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:40.290
Resplendent, elaborate, and it's even
adorned with multiple magecraft crests.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:38.130
<b><i>Protection</i></b>

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:40.330
<b><i>Multiple-Wall</i></b>

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:40.330
<b><i>Sanctum Barrier</i></b>

00:15:40.420 --> 00:15:42.210
Is that so amazing?

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:47.830
It enhances the outer wall as a protective barrier,
but also has a barrier that functions internally.

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:49.500
It's a highly efficient setup.

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:50.710
Of course.

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:55.580
Only a select few have the skill to activate it effectively.

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:57.670
Like Archbishop Orwell.

00:15:57.880 --> 00:16:01.460
Well, thank you for your kind words, Miss Menou.

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:03.290
Archbishop Orwell!

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.000
Please forgive me for not noticing.

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:07.000
No need to be so formal.

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:09.580
I'm so glad we finally get to meet, Miss Menou.

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:12.750
I heard there was trouble on the train?

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:15.290
Yes. I'm sorry for the worry.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:16.960
I'm just glad you're all right.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:18.290
Then you must be...

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.750
M-my name is Akari Tokitou!

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:23.000
Nice to meet you, I'm Orwell.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:24.920
I've heard about your situation.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:28.460
How awful it must have been to be
suddenly summoned to another world!

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:30.960
No, it honestly wasn't anything!

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:32.420
Rest assured...

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:37.460
The preparations for the ritual that will
send you home are coming along just fine.

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:39.920
We should be able to hold it two days from now, at noon.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.670
A-ah! I do appreciate it so deeply much!

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.040
Akari! Your words are coming out all wrong!

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:49.750
By the way, what do you intend to do
once the ritual is over, Miss Menou?

00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:52.880
If you're planning to take the
Pilgrimage Route along the border,

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:55.170
the Church can cover your pilgrimage expenses.

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:58.130
What, really?! Thank you very much!

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:03.460
But, if you would like to be helpful in return,
I'd like to ask you a favor.

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:05.290
What is it?

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:09.000
Do you remember the incidents happening
in Garm I told you about?

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:13.580
Yes. I believe you said that a series of
young women have gone missing.

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:14.920
Exactly, so...

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:19.420
I was hoping you could look
into it until the ritual is ready.

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:22.420
Do you think I'll be of any help?

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:25.420
I need a different perspective on it.

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:28.460
If you don't end up finding anything, that's fine.

00:17:28.670 --> 00:17:32.130
All right. If you say so, Archbishop.

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:35.330
Thank you. I'm counting on you, Miss Menou.

00:17:37.170 --> 00:17:39.750
Wow, what a nice room!

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:42.420
The Archbishop must have pulled some strings for us.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:51.580
Akari?

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:52.880
What?

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:54.630
Are you mad about something?

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.880
That's right, I'm mad.

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:58.710
Um...

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:00.830
Why?

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:03.710
We promised it would be a date!

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:07.540
You said we would go sight-seeing together,

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:10.630
but then you went and promised that
archbishop lady something else!

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:13.000
You mean the investigation? But that-

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:16.880
In return, you're getting money for
some pilgrimage thingy, aren't you?

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.290
Of course that's more important to you.

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:20.500
Listen, Akari-

00:18:20.500 --> 00:18:21.750
I know!

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:25.790
To you, that lady's an important
person you respect, right?

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:30.210
But me, I'm just some stranger passing
by who's going to be gone soon!

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.580
I didn't mean it like that-

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.040
Hmph! Whatever!

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:36.040
I'm going to take a bath!

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:43.290
The day after tomorrow, Akari will be...

00:18:45.710 --> 00:18:48.000
Jeez! Stupid Menou!

00:18:58.380 --> 00:19:00.380
I'm the stupid one...

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:03.830
Menou? Did you want me?

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:08.420
Hmm, a series of disappearances, huh?

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:12.080
You think human trafficking is
rampant in this city or something?

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:14.790
Apparently not. They've investigated that already.

00:19:14.920 --> 00:19:19.500
Then maybe some heretic is collecting
material to summon a demon?

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:23.380
It does feel like an Original Sin
might be involved somehow.

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.830
I want you to look into that side of things.

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:30.460
Hmm. Well, I don't mind helping out, of course.

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:34.210
While I'm investigating this, what will you be doing?

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.170
Uh?! Well...

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:40.580
Akari and I are uh... going sight-seeing...

00:19:40.580 --> 00:19:42.170
But of course you are!

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:47.670
You can't bring that useless set of boobs
along with you to do any kind of investigation!

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:51.130
Uhhh, that's right. I'm glad you understand...

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:52.460
Momo...

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:04.380
I love you so much that I'll do anything you ask me to do.

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:07.250
Thank you, Momo.

00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:11.670
I'll get this done in no time, just you wait!

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:12.790
Hey, Momo!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:17.170
The primary red gems that those
terrorists were told to swallow...

00:20:17.170 --> 00:20:20.290
They were probably provided by
someone with magecraft expertise.

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:24.420
The terrorists hinted that they could get
away as long as they got to Garm.

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:29.790
If whoever conspired with them is in Garm,
maybe that's where the red gems came from as well.

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:33.170
And that person might be one of
the Noblesse here in the city...

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:34.250
I take it?

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:38.670
I'm glad you're quick on the uptake.
Exactly. So be careful.

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:41.830
All right. I've got it, ma'am!

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:46.630
I always force the messy stuff on her plate.

00:20:54.630 --> 00:20:55.330
Akari...

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:57.290
What are you doing out here dressed like that?

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:59.130
I'm so sorry, Menou!

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:05.460
I know your work as a priestess is really important to you,
and I was insensitive.

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:11.000
Really, I'm sorry. I'll go sight-seeing by myself.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:13.460
Good luck with the job you have to do.

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:23.460
"Fun things are even better with two people," right?

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:29.420
Of course, if you'd rather go alone, that's fine too.

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:33.670
Of course not! I want to go with you, Menou!

00:21:33.670 --> 00:21:35.330
I swear. I swear!

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:36.920
Oh, Menou!

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:39.080
Okay, okay, I get it.

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:41.580
I get it so you can let go of me, Akari.

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:47.630
Uh, Akari. Your towel.

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.540
Flarette...

00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:59.380
That girl has the potential now...

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:01.830
Wouldn't you agree, Flare?

00:22:02.790 --> 00:22:05.380
Oh, my lower back hurts.

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:40.380
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:36.210 --> 00:23:40.380
<b>Goodbye</b>

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:39.710
Next episode: Goodbye.
